If youo have a chance to peek at the playground (the collection of level
files that is kept by your system as you leave individual levels), you'll
see that they are numbered.

Number 0 is general information about your character, numbers 1-27 (+/-)
are the Dungeons of Doom, numbers 27-50 is Gehennom, numbers 51-62 are the
Gnomish Mines, etc. (all numbers are examples, except 0 and 1). Likewise,
Sokoban, the Quest, Ludios, Vlad's Tower and the Planes are numbered. All
numbers used are consecutive.

You'll first have to figure out the order in which these numbers are given
out, then you should be able to notice when there's a gap in the numbers
used. For example, supposing the order I mention above is the real order
used by NetHack, if the top of the Quest is 67, and Vlad's tower is 69,
there should be a Fort Ludios. If those numbers are 68 nd 69, no such
level would exist.

This of course would be a mild form of cheating: you're using information
that isn't available to your character, but only outside of the game.

